TLD SHARED WORLD (ORTAK DÜNYA) - INSTALLING (version {V}, beta)
================================================================

A co-op mod for The Long Dark: play with friends in one shared world.
Not made or endorsed by Hinterland Studio. You need your own copy of the game.
Everyone needs the SAME game version number (e.g. 2.55) and the SAME mod version.
Steam and Epic players can play together. Epic's latest version is 2.55;
Steam players who want to play with an Epic friend roll back to 2.55
(see "Rolling Steam back to 2.55" on the mod's page).
Back up your saves before you try it:
  C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\Hinterland\TheLongDark
Türkçe: KURULUM.txt


EASY WAY: THE READY PACKAGE (recommended)
-----------------------------------------
"TLD-Shared-World-{V}-HAZIR-MelonLoader-dahil.zip" contains MelonLoader 0.7.3
and the mod; no installer needed.
 a) Close the game. Open the game folder (the one with tld.exe).
    Steam: right-click the game > Manage > Browse local files
    Epic : Library > the game's three dots > Manage > folder icon
 b) Delete if present: the MelonLoader folder, winhttp.dll, version.dll
 c) Copy what is INSIDE the zip into the game folder (winhttp.dll,
    MelonLoader, Mods, UserLibs; next to tld.exe).
 d) Start the game. A black window opens; the first start takes a few minutes.
Then go to 3) PLAYING. If something goes wrong, see 5) COMMON PROBLEMS.


INSTALLING BY HAND
==================

1) INSTALL MELONLOADER (once)
-----------------------------
 a) Download MelonLoader.Installer.exe:
    https://github.com/LavaGang/MelonLoader.Installer/releases
 b) Run it and pick "The Long Dark" (or "Add game" and point it to tld.exe
    in the game folder).
 c) Choose version 0.7.3 and press "Install".
 d) Start the game once and close it (the first start can take a few
    minutes and shows a black window full of text: that is normal).


2) INSTALL THE MOD
------------------
 a) Close the game.
 b) Double-click "install.bat" and answer its questions.
    By hand: copy Mods\TLDCoop.dll into the game's Mods folder and the
    three DLLs in UserLibs into the game's UserLibs folder.
 c) Start the game. The black window should list
    "TLD Shared World (Ortak Dunya)".


3) PLAYING
----------
Everything is in the game's menu: "CO-OP" in the main menu and the Esc menu.

HOST (the world's owner):
 - Load your own survival save.
 - Esc > CO-OP > HOST.
 - The same menu shows your address: "INTERNET: ..." (for a friend in
   another home) or "HOME NETWORK: ..." (same home). Choosing it copies it;
   send it to your friend.

JOINING FRIEND:
 - Copy the address your friend sent (Ctrl+C).
 - Main menu > CO-OP > "JOIN (COPIED): address" (or TYPE ADDRESS).
 - Wait for "SHARED WORLD READY", then open Survival > Load.
   The ORTAK DUNYA save opens by itself.

INTERNET: when you host, the mod asks your router to open UDP port 27500
(UPnP). If it says your router did not open it, turn on UPnP in the router
or forward UDP 27500 to this PC. If that is not possible, install the same
VPN on both PCs (Radmin VPN, Tailscale, Hamachi) and use its address.


4) KEYS
-------
 Esc > CO-OP     host, join, copy your address, leave, feedback
 F9 / F10 / F11  shortcuts: host / join / leave
 F6   status, your address and the key list
 F3   revive a downed friend (hold 5 s) / give up while down (hold 3 s)
 F8   get up while the others are not asleep yet; finish a long job now
 T    push to talk     B  whistle     V  give what is in your hands
      (or the item selected in the inventory)
 (if the game already uses B or V, the mod picks a free key and tells you)

Settings: UserData\MelonPreferences.cfg in the game folder, under [TLDCoop].
For example: DostAtesi = false (no friendly fire), IsSuresi = false (long
jobs do not wait), SesliKonusma = false (no voice), Dil = tr (Turkish).


5) COMMON PROBLEMS
------------------
 - The game starts without a black window: MelonLoader is missing or wrongly
   installed (no net6 folder in MelonLoader, net35/net472 instead). Use the
   READY PACKAGE. If it still happens, your antivirus may delete winhttp.dll:
   Windows Security > Virus & threat protection > Protection history.
 - Red text in the black window: "Application Control policy has blocked
   this file (0x800711C7)": Windows 11's Smart App Control blocks the files
   MelonLoader makes. Windows Security > App & browser control > Smart App
   Control settings > Off. (It is a security setting and your call; Windows
   may say it cannot be turned back on.)
 - On Epic the game sits on its loading screen: Epic may have opened a
   "cloud save conflict" window behind it. Bring the Epic Games Launcher to
   the front; to keep your newer local save choose "UPLOAD TO CLOUD".
 - "Error Generating Interop Assemblies" after rolling Steam back to 2.55:
   delete <game folder>\MelonLoader\Dependencies\Il2CppAssemblyGenerator\Cpp2IL\cpp2il_out
   and start the game again.
 - "Versions do not match": the game version in the corner of both main
   menus must be the same (Steam ends in S, Epic in E; that part is fine).


6) KNOWN ISSUES
---------------
 - First sessions between two homes over the internet are done; it is
   still a beta.
 - Death: if no friend lifts you within 10 minutes you die; your gear stays
   where you fell and you carry on without it. If nobody is left standing
   (everyone is down), the game ends after 30 seconds and the shared world
   save is deleted by the game's own rule.
 - Ground items (sticks and the like) follow the host's game when you enter
   a region or building; something you dropped in the last 30 seconds is kept.
 - Tested with 2 players; 3-4 players not tried yet (the server takes 4).
 - No password: while your server is open, anyone with your address and the
   mod can join. Share it only with friends and stop the server afterwards.
 - Playing over the internet needs UPnP, port forwarding or a VPN.
 - Different game or mod versions are refused; a game update can break the
   mod until a new version is out.
 - Survival mode only; no story mode; challenges and Tales not tested.
 - The world lives in the host's save; without the host there is no
   shared world to play in.
 - Long jobs take real time (a 2-hour job is about 10 minutes): the
   progress bar lasts that long.
 - Your friend is drawn with the mod's own model; clothes by kind and
   colour, simple animations.
 - Voice uses Windows' default microphone and speakers, no echo or noise
   filtering.
 - Ctrl+V in the address box is untested (JOIN (COPIED) does the same job).
 - No in-game settings screen; the mod is in English and Turkish only.


